    "LF127_130": "     If an STS(v) admits a χ′ (v)-coloring, then it is said to be minimum colorable, denoted\nby mcSTS(v). If v ≡ 3 (mod 6), then an mcSTS(v) is a KTS(v). An SQS(v) with minimum\ncolorable derived designs, abbreviated to mcDSQS(v), refers to an SQS(v) whose derived design\nat every point is minimum colorable. Therefore, an mcDSQS(v) is the same as an RDSQS(v)",
    "LF110": "\fGenerally, χ′ (v) equals (v + 1)/2 if v ≡ 1 (mod 6) and v ∈/ {7, 13} (see [19]). To sum up,",
    "formula": "chi-prime(73)=(73+1)/2=37. Independently D=73*72/6=876, M=floor(73/3)=24, ceil(D/M)=37; 36*24=864<876."
